      "title": "👑 Pixaroma - Note - START HERE",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# MODELS AND NODES USED IN THIS WORKFLOW  \n\n---\n\n### Models are downloaded automatically the first time you use the workflow.\n \n---\n\n## 🧩 Nodes Installed from Manager  \n\n- ComfyUI-Easy-Use\n- Qwen3-TTS - Voice Synthesis & Cloning\n- ComfyUI_LayerStyle\n\nRead More about Qwen TTS Node [HERE](https://github.com/flybirdxx/ComfyUI-Qwen-TTS)\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Resources  \n🎥 **Tutorials:** [Pixaroma YouTube Channel](https://www.youtube.com/@pixaroma)  \n💬 **Community Discord:** [Join Here](https://discord.com/invite/gggpkVgBf3)\n\n---\n\n## 🎙️ Qwen3 Voice Clone Workflow\n\n### What it does\n- Uses a **voice sample** (reference audio) to copy the voice\n- Speaks your **Speech Text** in that same voice\n- Saves an MP3\n\n### How to use (matches this workflow order)\n1. **Load Voice Sample (10–20s)**: choose a clean voice sample (one speaker, no music/noise, max 60s).\n2. **Reference Audio Text (Must Match Voice Sample Audio)**: paste the exact words spoken in the voice sample (recommended for best quality).\n3. **Speech Text**: type what you want the cloned voice to say.\n4. **VoiceClone settings**:\n   - **model_choice**: 0.6B (fast) or 1.7B (higher quality)\n   - **language**: Auto (or pick English/Chinese for best accuracy)\n5. Click **Run**\n\n### Save location\n- Preview inside **Save Audio (MP3)**\n- File saves under: **ComfyUI\\\\output\\\\audio**"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
